# Who must approve what (SEC-K, #847; Jonathan's decisions of 15/11 and 18/11): the files that a
# workflow holding a secret, a write permission or an OIDC token runs, the CD of Imladris, and the
# bench's Terraform — nothing else, so that every other pull request merges as before, without
# waiting for anyone.
#
# Not here, by decision (18/11): the Makefile. Its recipes run with the maintainer's own rights. What
# of them runs sudo on Imladris, or decides which host key ssh trusts, lives in scripts owned here
# (Jonathan's decision of 19/11), the targets only calling them with what the Makefile computes:
#   - the installation of the CD, `make imladris-cd-install`: infra/glorfindel-host/cd/install_from_workstation.sh
#     (CDI1, #918);
#   - the CD's timer turned on or off, the CD removed (`make imladris-cd-enable`, -cd-disable,
#     -cd-uninstall, sudo in a TTY): infra/glorfindel-host/cd/sudo_from_workstation.sh (CDI2, #922);
#   - the host key's check, `make imladris-known` (and orodruin-known): infra/glorfindel-host/known_host.sh;
#   - the SSH options toward Imladris (HOST_SSH_OPTS, so HOST_SSH): infra/glorfindel-host/ssh_opts.sh, whose
#     `check` each of these scripts runs itself before any gesture — the pinned form word for word, the
#     dedicated known_hosts, not empty, holding Imladris's key — instead of believing the Makefile.
# What stays, assumed: a hostile Makefile may no longer call these scripts, and run its own ssh, sudo
# included. That is assumed: the recipes run with the maintainer's rights, on his workstation, and he
# reads what he runs. The other recipes toward Imladris (push, start, stop, logs, the CD's check,
# status, retry, rollback…) run through HOST_SSH, their remote commands written in the Makefile, as the
# VM's user — a member of the docker group, which is as good as root (`docker run -v /:/h …`;
# infra/glorfindel-host/main.tf, required by cd/install.sh), and probably given a passwordless sudo by
# cloud-init on Azure's Ubuntu image (not measured). No sudo is written in the Makefile, but a docker
# command there can do as much: this lot closes the written sudo and the key's pinning, not that way.
# Orodruin's SSH options (SSH_OPTS, ORO_SSH) also stay in the Makefile, no owned script; only
# orodruin-known goes through known_host.sh. All assumed alike, for the same reason.
# docs/design/modele-de-menace.md, §7.
#
# It holds once the maintainer has turned on « Require review from Code Owners » in main's rule —
# after this file is merged, never before (with the former `*` line, every pull request would have
# waited for him). Then a pull request that touches one of these paths waits for his approval: the
# sessions' App, which has no Workflows right, can no longer change unseen what runs with the
# secrets by changing a script outside .github/workflows/. Until then, it is indicative only.
#
# tests/unit/test_codeowners.py keeps this list against the workflows: it reads each job of
# .github/workflows/ that holds a secret, a write permission or `id-token: write`, takes the files of
# the repository it runs (named in a `run:`, a local action, the code of a sparse checkout, a
# requirements file it installs, what a script imports next to it or a shell script calls next to
# it), adds what Imladris's CD installs (AGENT_FILES) and the scripts the Makefile's recipes toward
# Imladris call (WORKSTATION: the bash scripts of imladris-known, of the CD's recipes and of
# HOST_SSH_OPTS, and what they call), and fails when one of them has no line here — or when a line owns
# none of them, but the four directories owned whole (DECIDED in the test). The form it reads: one
# owner, the maintainer; an anchored path, a file or a directory (a trailing /), no pattern.
# docs/design/modele-de-menace.md, §6 and §7.

# The CI itself, this file included.
/.github/                               @grootcyber

# publish.yml: the OIDC token that signs the images, packages: write, attestations: write.
/scripts/published_image.py             @grootcyber
/scripts/image_check.py                 @grootcyber
/scripts/retry.sh                       @grootcyber

# notify.yml, roadmap.yml: the Discord secrets of the workshop (its sparse checkout, all of it).
/scripts/notify_discord.py              @grootcyber
/scripts/roadmap_discord.py             @grootcyber
/glorfindel/chat_text.py                @grootcyber
/.claude/skills/elrond/palantir.py      @grootcyber

# pip-audit.yml: issues: write — the script, and the lock of the pip-audit it installs.
/scripts/pip_audit_issues.py            @grootcyber
/requirements/audit.txt                 @grootcyber

# canary-azurerm.yml: the canary's OIDC token (Network Contributor on its group).
/infra/canary/                          @grootcyber

# The CD of Imladris, and what it installs next to it (AGENT_FILES).
/infra/glorfindel-host/cd/              @grootcyber
/infra/glorfindel-host/deploy.sh        @grootcyber

# What the Makefile calls to reach Imladris from the maintainer's workstation (CDI2, #922): the host
# key's check, and the SSH options that pin it. The CD's recipes that run sudo there are under cd/.
/infra/glorfindel-host/known_host.sh    @grootcyber
/infra/glorfindel-host/ssh_opts.sh      @grootcyber

# The bench's Terraform (decision of 18/11): its local-exec provisioners run with the rights of
# whoever applies, at `terraform apply`, and never show in the plan.
/infra/terraform/                       @grootcyber
